dualToIdeal -- dual ideal
*************************

  * Usage: 
        dualToIdeal(I)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the dual of I

Description
===========

Takes an ideal I as input, dualizes the ideal, and maps it back into the ring,
producing Hom_R(I,R) ~ J < R.  Used to produce the global sections H^0(mD),
where D is an integral divisor defined by I.



