globallyGenerated -- globallyGenerated(D) produces a smallest integer a such that O_X(aD) is globally generated.
****************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        globallyGenerated(D)
        globallyGenerated(I)
        globallyGenerated(M)
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note WeilDivisor:
        (WeilDivisors)BasicDivisor,,
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, 

Description
===========

Takes a divisor as input.  It then uses a binary search to check for the
smallest integer a with the property that |aD| is a basepoint-free linear
series.  In this case, the corresponding line bundle is globally generated.



